</tbody></table><div class="templateVersion l version-legend" style="" about="#mwt941"><div style=""><span style="white-space: nowrap;"><b>Legend:</b></span></div><div style="display: flex;" class="legend-item"><span class="swatch swatch-unsupported"></span>Unsupported</div><div style="display: flex;" class="legend-item"><span class="swatch swatch-maintained"></span>Supported</div><div style="display: flex;" class="legend-item"><span class="swatch swatch-latest"></span><b>Latest version</b></div><div style="display: none;" class="legend-item"><span class="swatch swatch-preview"></span>Preview version</div><div style="display: none;" class="legend-item"><span class="swatch swatch-future"></span>Future version</div></div><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1295599781" about="#mwt941" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Version/styles.css"}}'/><span about="#mwt941">
</span><p about="#mwt941"><b>Notes</b></p><ul about="#mwt941"><li><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_for_iOS" title="Firefox for iOS" class="mw-redirect">Firefox for iOS</a> is not listed in this table as its version numbers would be misleading. Prior to version 96,<sup about="#mwt1031" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-237" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-237"}}'><a href="#cite_note-237" id="mwBk8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBlA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlE">[</span>237<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlI">]</span></span></a></sup> it used version numbers distinct from other Firefox versions, which share the core <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(software)" title="Gecko (software)">Gecko</a> rendering engine. The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOS" title="IOS">iOS</a> app uses the operating system's rendering engine (<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebKit" title="WebKit">WebKit</a>), rather than Mozilla's (Gecko).</li></ul>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="22" id="mwBlM" aria-labelledby="Firefox_for_iOS"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Firefox_for_iOS">Firefox for iOS</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Firefox&amp;action=edit&amp;section=22" title="Edit section: Firefox for iOS"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<figure class="mw-halign-right" typeof="mw:File/Thumb" id="mwBlQ"><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png" class="mw-file-description" id="mwBlU"><img resource="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png" src="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png/250px-Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail" decoding="async" loading="lazy" srcset="//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ed/Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png/500px-Firefox_for_iOS_144_screenshot.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x" data-file-width="1179" data-file-height="2556" data-file-type="bitmap" height="412" width="190" class="mw-file-element" id="mwBlY"/></a><figcaption id="mwBlc">Firefox 144 on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOS" title="IOS" id="mwBlg">iOS</a></figcaption></figure>
<p id="mwBlk">Mozilla initially refused to port Firefox to iOS due to the restrictions Apple imposed on third-party iOS browsers. Instead of releasing a full version of the Firefox browser, Mozilla released Firefox Home, a companion app for the iPhone and iPod Touch based on the Firefox Sync technology, which allowed users to access their Firefox browsing history, bookmarks, and recent tabs. It also included Firefox's "Awesomebar" location bar. Firefox Home was not a web browser, the application launched web pages in either an embedded viewer for that one page, or by opening the page in the Safari app.<sup about="#mwt1036" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-238" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-238"}}'><a href="#cite_note-238" id="mwBlo"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBls"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBlw">[</span>238<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBl0">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1039" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-239" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-239"}}'><a href="#cite_note-239" id="mwBl4"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBl8"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmA">[</span>239<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmE">]</span></span></a></sup> Mozilla pulled Firefox Home from the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/App_Store_(Apple)" title="App Store (Apple)" id="mwBmI">App Store</a> in September 2012, stating it would focus its resources on other projects. The company subsequently released the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Source_code" title="Source code" id="mwBmM">source code</a> of Firefox Home's underlying synchronization software.<sup about="#mwt1042" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-CW_240-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"CW"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CW-240"}}'><a href="#cite_note-CW-240" id="mwBmQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBmU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmY">[</span>240<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBmc">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBmg">In April 2013, then-Mozilla CEO <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gary_Kovacs" title="Gary Kovacs" id="mwBmk">Gary Kovacs</a> said that Firefox would not come to iOS if Apple required the use of the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebKit" title="WebKit" id="mwBmo">WebKit</a> layout engine to do so. One reason given by Mozilla was that before <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IOS_8" title="IOS 8" id="mwBms">iOS 8</a>, Apple had supplied third-party browsers with an inferior version of its JavaScript engine, which hobbled their performance, making it impossible to match Safari's JavaScript performance on the iOS platform.<sup about="#mwt1045" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-241" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241"}}'><a href="#cite_note-241" id="mwBmw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBm0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm4">[</span>241<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBm8">]</span></span></a></sup> Apple later opened their "Nitro" JavaScript engine to third-party browsers.<sup about="#mwt1048" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-242" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-242"}}'><a href="#cite_note-242" id="mwBnA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnI">[</span>242<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnM">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2015, Mozilla announced it was moving forward with Firefox for iOS, with a preview release made available in New Zealand in September of that year.<sup about="#mwt1051" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-243" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-243"}}'><a href="#cite_note-243" id="mwBnQ"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnU"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnY">[</span>243<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBnc">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1054" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-244" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244"}}'><a href="#cite_note-244" id="mwBng"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBnk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBno">[</span>244<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBns">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1057" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-245" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-245"}}'><a href="#cite_note-245" id="mwBnw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBn0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn4">[</span>245<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBn8">]</span></span></a></sup> It was fully released in November later that year.<sup about="#mwt1060" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-246" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-246"}}'><a href="#cite_note-246" id="mwBoA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBoE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoI">[</span>246<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoM">]</span></span></a></sup> It is the first Firefox-branded browser not to use the <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gecko_(layout_engine)" title="Gecko (layout engine)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBoQ">Gecko</a> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Browser_engine" title="Browser engine" id="mwBoU">layout engine</a> as is used in Firefox for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mozilla_Firefox" title="Mozilla Firefox" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBoY">desktop</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_for_mobile" title="Firefox for mobile" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBoc">mobile</a>. Apple's policies require all iOS apps that browse the web to use the built-in WebKit rendering framework and WebKit JavaScript, so using Gecko is not possible.<sup about="#mwt1063" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-247" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-247"}}'><a href="#cite_note-247" id="mwBog"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBok"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBoo">[</span>247<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBos">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1066" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-248" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248"}}'><a href="#cite_note-248" id="mwBow"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBo0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo4">[</span>248<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBo8">]</span></span></a></sup> Unlike <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_for_Android" title="Firefox for Android" id="mwBpA">Firefox on Android</a>, Firefox for iOS does not support browser add-ons.</p>

<p id="mwBpE">In November 2016, Firefox released a new iOS app titled <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_Focus" title="Firefox Focus" id="mwBpI">Firefox Focus</a>, a private web browser.<sup about="#mwt1069" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-249" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-249"}}'><a href="#cite_note-249" id="mwBpM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpU">[</span>249<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBpY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="23" id="mwBpc" aria-labelledby="Firefox_Reality_(AR/VR)"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Firefox_Reality_(AR/VR)"><span id="Firefox_Reality_.28AR.2FVR.29" typeof="mw:FallbackId"></span>Firefox Reality (AR/VR)</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Firefox&amp;action=edit&amp;section=23" title="Edit section: Firefox Reality (AR/VR)"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBpg">Firefox Reality was released for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Augmented_reality" title="Augmented reality" id="mwBpk">augmented reality</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_reality" title="Virtual reality" id="mwBpo">virtual reality</a> headsets in September 2018.<sup about="#mwt1072" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FirefoxReality_250-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"FirefoxReality"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FirefoxReality-250"}}'><a href="#cite_note-FirefoxReality-250" id="mwBps"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBpw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp0">[</span>250<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBp4">]</span></span></a></sup> It supports traditional web-browsing through 2D windows and immersive VR pages through <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/WebVR" title="WebVR" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBp8">Web VR</a>. Firefox Reality is available on <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HTC_Vive" title="HTC Vive" id="mwBqA">HTC Vive</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oculus_(brand)" title="Oculus (brand)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBqE">Oculus</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Daydream" title="Google Daydream" id="mwBqI">Google Daydream</a> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Hololens" title="Microsoft Hololens" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBqM">Microsoft Hololens</a> headsets. In February 2022, Mozilla announced that <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Igalia" title="Igalia" id="mwBqQ">Igalia</a> took over stewardship of this project under the new name of Wolvic.<sup about="#mwt1075" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-251" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-251"}}'><a href="#cite_note-251" id="mwBqU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBqY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqc">[</span>251<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBqg">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

</section><section data-mw-section-id="24" id="mwBqk" aria-labelledby="Third-party_ports"><div class="mw-heading mw-heading3"><h3 id="Third-party_ports">Third-party ports</h3><span class="mw-editsection"><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">[</span><a href="/w/index.php?title=Firefox&amp;action=edit&amp;section=24" title="Edit section: Third-party ports"><span>edit</span></a><span class="mw-editsection-bracket">]</span></span></div>
<p id="mwBqo">Firefox has also been ported to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FreeBSD" title="FreeBSD" id="mwBqs">FreeBSD</a>,<sup about="#mwt1078" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-FreeBSD_252-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"FreeBSD"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FreeBSD-252"}}'><a href="#cite_note-FreeBSD-252" id="mwBqw"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBq0"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq4">[</span>252<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBq8">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NetBSD" title="NetBSD" id="mwBrA">NetBSD</a>,<sup about="#mwt1081" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-NetBSD1_253-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"NetBSD1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NetBSD1-253"}}'><a href="#cite_note-NetBSD1-253" id="mwBrE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrM">[</span>253<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrQ">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenBSD" title="OpenBSD" id="mwBrU">OpenBSD</a>,<sup about="#mwt1084" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OpenBSD_254-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"OpenBSD"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OpenBSD-254"}}'><a href="#cite_note-OpenBSD-254" id="mwBrY"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrc"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrg">[</span>254<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBrk">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenIndiana" title="OpenIndiana" id="mwBro">OpenIndiana</a>,<sup about="#mwt1086" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-OpenIndiana_255-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"OpenIndiana"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-OpenIndiana-255"}}'><a href="#cite_note-OpenIndiana-255" id="mwBrs"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBrw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr0">[</span>255<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBr4">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OS/2" title="OS/2" id="mwBr8">OS/2</a>,<sup about="#mwt1089" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-256" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-256"}}'><a href="#cite_note-256" id="mwBsA"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsE"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsI">[</span>256<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsM">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ArcaOS" title="ArcaOS" id="mwBsQ">ArcaOS</a>,<sup about="#mwt1092" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-257" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-257"}}'><a href="#cite_note-257" id="mwBsU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsc">[</span>257<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBsg">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SkyOS" title="SkyOS" id="mwBsk">SkyOS</a>, <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RISC_OS" title="RISC OS" id="mwBso">RISC OS</a><sup about="#mwt1095" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-258" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-258"}}'><a href="#cite_note-258" id="mwBss"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBsw"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs0">[</span>258<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBs4">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BeOS" title="BeOS" id="mwBs8">BeOS</a>/<a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Haiku_(operating_system)" title="Haiku (operating system)" id="mwBtA">Haiku</a>,<sup about="#mwt1098" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-259" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-259"}}'><a href="#cite_note-259" id="mwBtE"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtI"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtM">[</span>259<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtQ">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1101" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BeBytes_260-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BeBytes"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BeBytes-260"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BeBytes-260" id="mwBtU"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBtY"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtc">[</span>260<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtg">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1104" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BeBits1_261-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BeBits1"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BeBits1-261"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BeBits1-261" id="mwBtk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBto"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBts">[</span>261<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBtw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1107" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-BeBits2_262-0" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{"name":"BeBits2"},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-BeBits2-262"}}'><a href="#cite_note-BeBits2-262" id="mwBt0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBt4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBt8">[</span>262<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuA">]</span></span></a></sup> and an unofficial rebranded version called <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timberwolf_(web_browser)" title="Timberwolf (web browser)" id="mwBuE">Timberwolf</a> has been available for <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AmigaOS_4" title="AmigaOS 4" id="mwBuI">AmigaOS 4</a>.<sup about="#mwt1110" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-263" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-263"}}'><a href="#cite_note-263" id="mwBuM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuU">[</span>263<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuY">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBuc">The Firefox port for OpenBSD has been maintained by Landry Breuil since 2010. Firefox is regularly built for the current branch of the operating system; the latest versions are packaged for each release and remain frozen until the next release. In 2017, Landry began hosting packages of newer Firefox versions for OpenBSD releases from 6.0 onwards, making them available to installations without the ports system.<sup about="#mwt1113" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-264" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-264"}}'><a href="#cite_note-264" id="mwBug"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBuk"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBuo">[</span>264<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBus">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

<p id="mwBuw">The <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solaris_(operating_system)" title="Solaris (operating system)" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBu0">Solaris</a> 10 port of Firefox (including <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenSolaris" title="OpenSolaris" id="mwBu4">OpenSolaris</a>) was maintained by the Oracle Solaris Desktop Beijing Team,<sup about="#mwt1116" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-265" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265"}}'><a href="#cite_note-265" id="mwBu8"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvA"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvE">[</span>265<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvI">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1119" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-266" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-266"}}'><a href="#cite_note-266" id="mwBvM"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvQ"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvU">[</span>266<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvY">]</span></span></a></sup> until March 2018 when the team was disbanded. There was also an unofficial port of <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Firefox_3.6" title="Firefox 3.6" class="mw-redirect" id="mwBvc">Firefox 3.6</a>.x to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_AIX" title="IBM AIX" id="mwBvg">IBM AIX</a><sup about="#mwt1122" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-267" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-267"}}'><a href="#cite_note-267" id="mwBvk"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBvo"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvs">[</span>267<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBvw">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about="#mwt1125" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-268" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-268"}}'><a href="#cite_note-268" id="mwBv0"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBv4"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBv8">[</span>268<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwA">]</span></span></a></sup> and of v1.7.x to <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/UnixWare" title="UnixWare" id="mwBwE">UnixWare</a>.<sup about="#mwt1128" class="mw-ref reference" id="cite_ref-269" rel="dc:references" typeof="mw:Extension/ref" data-mw='{"name":"ref","attrs":{},"body":{"id":"mw-reference-text-cite_note-269"}}'><a href="#cite_note-269" id="mwBwI"><span class="mw-reflink-text" id="mwBwM"><span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwQ">[</span>269<span class="cite-bracket" id="mwBwU">]</span></span></a></sup></p>

