<li about="#cite_note-111" id="cite_note-111" data-mw-footnote-number="111"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD0k"><a href="#cite_ref-111" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD0o"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD0s">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-111" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt394" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD0w" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"Cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Captain"},"first":{"wt":"Sean"},"date":{"wt":"11 August 2019"},"title":{"wt":"Firefox at 15: its rise, fall, and privacy-first renaissance"},"url":{"wt":"https://www.fastcompany.com/90428050/firefox-at-15-its-rise-fall-and-privacy-first-renaissance"},"access-date":{"wt":"6 June 2024"},"website":{"wt":"[[Fast Company]]"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20200507110319/https://www.fastcompany.com/90428050/firefox-at-15-its-rise-fall-and-privacy-first-renaissance"},"archive-date":{"wt":"May 7, 2020"},"url-status":{"wt":"live"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCaptain2019" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt394">Captain, Sean (August 11, 2019). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://www.fastcompany.com/90428050/firefox-at-15-its-rise-fall-and-privacy-first-renaissance" class="external text" id="mwD00">"Firefox at 15: its rise, fall, and privacy-first renaissance"</a>. <i id="mwD04"><a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fast_Company" title="Fast Company" id="mwD08">Fast Company</a></i>. <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20200507110319/https://www.fastcompany.com/90428050/firefox-at-15-its-rise-fall-and-privacy-first-renaissance" class="external text" id="mwD1A">Archived</a> from the original on May 7, 2020<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD1E">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD1I">June 6,</span> 2024</span>.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Fast+Company&amp;rft.atitle=Firefox+at+15%3A+its+rise%2C+fall%2C+and+privacy-first+renaissance&amp;rft.date=2019-08-11&amp;rft.aulast=Captain&amp;rft.aufirst=Sean&amp;rft_id=https%3A%2F%2Fwww.fastcompany.com%2F90428050%2Ffirefox-at-15-its-rise-fall-and-privacy-first-renaissance&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AFirefox" class="Z3988" about="#mwt394" id="mwD1M"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-WSJHowTo2-112" id="cite_note-WSJHowTo2-112" data-mw-footnote-number="112"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD1Q"><a href="#cite_ref-WSJHowTo2_112-0" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD1U"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD1Y">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-WSJHowTo2-112" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt397" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD1c" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Mossberg"},"first":{"wt":"Walter S."},"date":{"wt":"September 16, 2004"},"title":{"wt":"How to Protect Yourself From Vandals, Viruses If You Use Windows"},"url":{"wt":"http://ptech.wsj.com/archive/ptech-20040916.html"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20070221061526/http://ptech.wsj.com/archive/ptech-20040916.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"February 21, 2007"},"access-date":{"wt":"October 17, 2006"},"work":{"wt":"The Wall Street Journal"},"quote":{"wt":"I suggest dumping Microsoft&apos;s Internet Explorer Web browser, which has a history of security breaches. I recommend instead Mozilla Firefox, which is free at mozilla.org. It&apos;s not only more secure but also more modern and advanced, with tabbed browsing, which allows multiple pages to be open on one screen, and a better pop-up ad blocker than the belated one Microsoft recently added to IE."}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="mwD1g" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt397" data-x-id="CITEREFMossberg2004">Mossberg, Walter S. (September 16, 2004). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20070221061526/http://ptech.wsj.com/archive/ptech-20040916.html" class="external text" id="mwD1k">"How to Protect Yourself From Vandals, Viruses If You Use Windows"</a>. <i id="mwD1o">The Wall Street Journal</i>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://ptech.wsj.com/archive/ptech-20040916.html" class="external text" data-mw-original-href="http://ptech.wsj.com/archive/ptech-20040916.html" id="mwD1s">the original</a> on February 21, 2007<span class="reference-accessdate" id="mwD1w">. Retrieved <span class="nowrap" id="mwD10">October 17,</span> 2006</span>. <q id="mwD14">I suggest dumping Microsoft's Internet Explorer Web browser, which has a history of security breaches. I recommend instead Mozilla Firefox, which is free at mozilla.org. It's not only more secure but also more modern and advanced, with tabbed browsing, which allows multiple pages to be open on one screen, and a better pop-up ad blocker than the belated one Microsoft recently added to IE.</q></cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=The+Wall+Street+Journal&amp;rft.atitle=How+to+Protect+Yourself+From+Vandals%2C+Viruses+If+You+Use+Windows&amp;rft.date=2004-09-16&amp;rft.aulast=Mossberg&amp;rft.aufirst=Walter+S.&amp;rft_id=http%3A%2F%2Fptech.wsj.com%2Farchive%2Fptech-20040916.html&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AFirefox" class="Z3988" about="#mwt397" id="mwD18"></span></span></li>
<li about="#cite_note-113" id="cite_note-113" data-mw-footnote-number="113"><span class="mw-cite-backlink" id="mwD2A"><a href="#cite_ref-113" rel="mw:referencedBy" id="mwD2E"><span class="mw-linkback-text" id="mwD2I">↑</span></a></span> <span id="mw-reference-text-cite_note-113" class="mw-reference-text reference-text"><link rel="mw-deduplicated-inline-style" href="mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106" about="#mwt400" typeof="mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion" id="mwD2M" data-mw='{"name":"templatestyles","attrs":{"src":"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css"},"body":{"extsrc":""},"parts":[{"template":{"target":{"wt":"cite news ","href":"./Template:Cite_news"},"params":{"last":{"wt":"Costa"},"first":{"wt":"Dan"},"date":{"wt":"March 24, 2005"},"editor-last":{"wt":"Vamosi"},"editor-first":{"wt":"Scott"},"title":{"wt":"Mozilla Firefox – Review"},"url":{"wt":"https://reviews.cnet.com/browsers/mozilla-firefox/4505-3514_7-31117280.html"},"archive-url":{"wt":"https://web.archive.org/web/20071226062127/http://reviews.cnet.com/browsers/mozilla-firefox/4505-3514_7-31117280.html"},"archive-date":{"wt":"December 26, 2007"},"publisher":{"wt":"[[CNET]]"}},"i":0}}]}'/><cite id="CITEREFCosta2005" class="citation news cs1" about="#mwt400">Costa, Dan (March 24, 2005). Vamosi, Scott (ed.). <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://web.archive.org/web/20071226062127/http://reviews.cnet.com/browsers/mozilla-firefox/4505-3514_7-31117280.html" class="external text" id="mwD2Q">"Mozilla Firefox – Review"</a>. <a rel="mw:WikiLink" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CNET" title="CNET" id="mwD2U">CNET</a>. Archived from <a rel="mw:ExtLink nofollow" href="https://reviews.cnet.com/browsers/mozilla-firefox/4505-3514_7-31117280.html" class="external text" id="mwD2Y">the original</a> on December 26, 2007.</cite><span title="ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.atitle=Mozilla+Firefox+%E2%80%93+Review&amp;rft.date=2005-03-24&amp;rf